==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*mreǵʰ-}}
First attested in English in 1509; either:
* Borrowed directly from {{bor|en|la|brevitās}}; or
* from {{der|en|xno|brevité}}, from {{der|en|fro|brieveté}}, from {{der|en|la|brevitātem}}, accusative of {{m|la|brevitās}}, from {{m|la|brevis||short}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɹɛvəti/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɹɛvəti/|[ˈbɹɛvəɾi]|a=US,CA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-brevity.ogg|a=Maryland}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɹevəti/|[ˈbɹevəɾi]|a=AU,NZ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The quality of being [[brief]] in duration.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005
|author=Bill Bryson
|title=A short history of nearly everything
|passage=Thanks to Global Positioning Systems we can see that Europe and North America are parting at about the speed a fingernail grows—roughly two yards in a human lifetime. If you were prepared to wait long enough, you could ride from Los Angeles all the way up to San Francisco. It is only the [[brevity]] of lifetimes that keeps us from appreciating the changes.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[succinctness|Succinctness]]; [[conciseness]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Hamlet|act=2|scene=2|passage='''[B]revity''' is the soul of wit,<br>And tediousness the limbs and outward flourishes[.]}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|passage=Whenever a public question comes to such a crisis that the opportunities for individual intervention are reduced to the smallest possible compass, Mr. Roebuck is sure to step in with a formula, summing up the case with indignant '''brevity''', censuring somebody, or [[panegyrizing]] somebody.|title=Head and Tail|work=The Saturday Review of Politics, Literature, Science, and Art|date=14 June 1856|pageurl=https://www.google.ca/books/edition/Saturday_Review_of_Politics_Literature_S/IHJJAQAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&pg=PA142|page=142|issue=33|volume=2|publisher=John W. Parker and Son|location=London}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1966
|author=Jackson E. Morris
|title=Principles of scientific and technical writing
|passage=A good technical writing style will now be defined as a style possessing clarity, '''brevity''', and variety.}}
# {{lb|en|rare|countable}} A short piece of writing.

====Synonyms====
